For growth with testosterone, dissolve testosterone in acetone (20 mg/ml) and  dispense portions of the solution, e.g., 0.1 ml portions for 10 ml medium, to anaerobic culture tubes. Let the solvent evaporate to dryness. Dispense 10 ml portions of medium in the culture tubes and stream with N<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (80:20, v/v). Close the vessels and autoclave. Treat the vessels in an ultrasonic bath to detach and suspend the testosterone.  <br>
For growth with heptanoate, omit testosterone. Sterilize the gassed medium in anaerobic vessels by autoclaving. Add 2.5 mM heptanoate from a 20-fold filter-sterilized anaerobic stock solution after cooling.  <br>
After autoclaving, add (per 10 ml) 0.3 ml NaHCO<sub>3</sub> solution (84 g/L, autoclaved under a CO<sub>2</sub> atmosphere), 1 &#181;l Trace element solution SL-10 (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=433">433</a>), 1 &#181;l Selenite-tungstate solution (see below) and 1 &#181;l Vitamin solution (see below). Adjust pH to 7.2. Incubate the cultures in the dark for up to 4 weeks. Briefly shake the cultures once per day.  <br>
<I>Selenite-tungstate solution:</I> <br>
